<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan soybean imports fall 11.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan soybean imports fall 11.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's soybean imports in January totalled 471,914 tonnes, down 11.7 percent on the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 Jan 97     Dec 96	Jan 96</p>
<p> Total imports     471,914    490,600     534,298</p>
<p>Major suppliers of soybeans (in tonnes):</p>
<p> U.S.		  442,383    405,780     510,916</p>
<p>Total imports in calendar 1996 reached 4.87 million tonnes against 4.81 million tonnes a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
